**Docs subagent returns.** I check every live-state sentence against its evidence file, then:

```bash
cd "$REPO/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs"
git grep -nE "code/session_[0-9A-Za-z]"        # empty
<the project's docs-only check from CLAUDE.md>
git push -u origin chore/wg-keepalive-docs-close
gh pr create --title "docs: close WireGuard keepalive relay" --body-file "$SCRATCH/pr-body-wg-docs.md"
gh pr merge <n> --merge --delete-branch
```

**Memory.** I write `wg-keepalive-relay-live-on-ccs-it.md` (type `project`) and its `MEMORY.md` pointer: PR #165, live on `ccs-it` since 2026-09-28, `ccs-ops` untouched, acceptance covered 3 minutes only.

**Backlog.** `docs closed: yes`, republish.

**Cleanup:**

```bash
herdr agent get wgka                           # idle, "focused": false
herdr tab close <wgka tab_id>
git -C "$REPO" worktree remove "$REPO/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive"
git -C "$REPO" worktree remove "$REPO/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs"
git -C "$REPO" worktree prune
git -C "$REPO" pull
git -C "$REPO" branch -d feat/wg-keepalive-relay chore/wg-keepalive-docs-close
kill 48211
git -C "$REPO" worktree list; ps -ax -o pid,command | grep -i '[c]odex'
```

Then backlog `done`, republish, status.

**A product-advisor waiter fires.** I read `.last`, then `herdr agent get`, then the context usage. Facts get answered with evidence. Every real choice becomes a neutral ballot to `adv-codex` and `adv-fable` at once. Round 2 goes out by file path.

## Why

- **"Accepted" is not `done`.** A task closes only with docs closed and cleanup finished. The snapshot still describes `ccs-it` before the relay, and the RDP audio design would be built on that wrong state.
- **The paperwork costs my session nothing.** A subagent writes it while the evidence is fresh, in a worktree, committed. After nine hours, "later" is how it never happens.
- **`wgka` is not reused.** One tab is one task, and no executor may exist before `brainstormed`. Its familiarity with the roles would carry the relay's assumptions into a design made alone. It stays open until the docs close, in case a claim needs checking, and then it closes.
- **RDP audio is a new task, so it enters at stage 0.** The design comes from two model families and a 2/2 vote. I hand over facts with evidence, no hints, because I design nothing.
- **"By morning" is a wish.** There is no time box and nothing is shortened. Nothing yet shows the full brainstorm cannot fit, so no poll is due. If that changes, slipping the deadline or waiving the brainstorm is the operator's choice.
- **No ballot or poll is needed now.** Everything here is routine: my own tabs, worktrees, a docs-only merge, and helpers I started.
- **The cleanup follows the pipeline order** — docs, backlog, cleanup — and I look at each target before deleting it.
- **Both tracks run in parallel on background waiters,** so neither the operator's request nor the closing work waits.
